  "description": "Declarative 2D spatial decomposition for spreadsheet-shaped data. Describe the shape of a sheet once — a header, a table, repeating blocks, a section under a caption — and Unrect decomposes the grid along that description and projects each part into typed objects. No cursors, no row loops, no index arithmetic: the shape is a value you can reuse across workbooks, and a failure names the declaration that failed and the cell it failed on. Includes the in-memory adapter for tests and scripts.",
  "id": "Unrect",
